<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis III, Duke of Brittany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1518–<a href="/years/1536">1536</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis III was duke of Brittany from 1524 to 1536, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-duke-of-nevers">Francis I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claude-of-france">Claude of France</a>, known as the Dauphin Francis. He was crowned duke at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a> in 1532, the year the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estates-of-brittany">Estates of Brittany</a> agreed to union with France. He died at Tournon in 1536, and the title passed to his brother, the future Henry II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-iii-duke-of-brittany.jpg" alt="Francis III, Duke of Brittany" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Corneille de Lyon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corneille_de_Lyon_-_Le_dauphin_Fran%C3%A7ois_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Cond%C3%A9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
